    "_postman_id": "b7e9c2a1-4f6d-4e3a-9c8b-2a1d5f7e9c01",
    "name": "ReadMeAI API — Full Routes",
    "description": "🚀 **ReadMeAI — AI README Generator**\n\nComplete Postman collection for testing **every** backend route of the ReadMeAI API (Node.js + Express + MongoDB + OpenAI).\n\n---\n\n### 🔑 How to use\n1. Start the API: `cd server && npm run dev` (port **4000**)\n2. (Optional) Seed demo data: `npm run seed`\n3. Run **Auth → Login (Demo User)** — the test script automatically saves the JWT into the `token` collection variable.\n4. All protected routes use `Authorization: Bearer {{token}}` (cookie `readmeai_token` also works automatically).\n5. For Admin routes, run **Auth → Login (Admin)** instead.\n\n### 📌 Variables\n| Variable | Purpose |\n| --- | --- |\n| `baseUrl` | API origin (default `http://localhost:4000`; set to `http://localhost:5173` to test through the Vite dev proxy) |\n| `token` | JWT saved automatically after Login / Register |\n| `readmeId` | Saved after **Generate README** |\n| `sessionId` | Chat session id (default `postman-session-1`) |\n| `notificationId` / `issueId` / `adminIssueId` | Saved automatically from list responses |\n\n> Demo creds → **demo@readmeai.dev / demo123456** · Admin creds → **admin@readmeai.local / admin12345**",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "readmeai"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
